# Buzz Wire Game Project

## Overview
This repository contains the source code for a **Buzz Wire game** implemented on an Arduino Uno (ATmega328P). The project includes modular C libraries for handling:

- **Input** (buttons and touch wire detection)
- **Output** (display and buzzer)
- **Game logic** (timing, win/lose conditions)
- **Utility functions** (millis timer, hardware timer management)

The game challenges the player to carefully guide a wire loop along a wire without touching it, measuring time and signaling success or failure with a buzzer and display.

## Technologies & Tools
- PlatformIO (build system and environment)
- AVR-GCC compiler targeting ATmega328P
- Arduino Uno hardware
- Modular C code organization with separate libraries (`buttons`, `buzzer`, `display`, `game_logic`, `millis`, `timer`)

## Progress Last Week
- Implemented core game logic including timer tracking with `millis()` and input handling for wire touch and goal detection.
- Created a timer display feature showing elapsed time in MMSS format on a 4-digit display.
- Developed functions to show temporary messages on the display.
- Refined hardware abstraction layers for buzzer and input pins using AVR registers.
- Added appropriate header file includes to resolve implicit function declaration warnings.
- Successfully built and linked the project with all libraries on PlatformIO for the Arduino Uno.
- Began integrating timer and buzzer modules with the main game loop for event-driven sound control.

